| `ENV_PRODUCTION` | The base64-encoded string of your production `.env` file. | (See below) |

> [!TIP]
> To easily generate the base64 string for the `ENV_PRODUCTION` secret, you can run the following command on your server or local machine:
> ```bash
> base64 -w 0 .env
> ```
> Copy the output and paste it directly as the secret's value.

Once these secrets are set, any push or merge into the `production` branch will trigger a seamless automated deployment!


# Custom Nepali Calendar Redesign

This plan outlines the redesign of the calendar interface to feature a custom, full-page Bikram Sambat (Nepali) calendar grid as per the provided reference image.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Dependencies
- **Install `nepali-date`**: Add this lightweight package to handle B.S. (Bikram Sambat) to A.D. (Gregorian) date conversions, determining the correct number of days per Nepali month, and extracting localized labels.

### 2. New Component: `NepaliCalendarGrid.vue`
We will create a new, reusable Vue component at `resources/js/Components/NepaliCalendarGrid.vue`. This component will:
- Generate a 7-column CSS grid.
- Map Nepali dates (e.g. Jestha 2083) to English dates.
- Display large Nepali numerals in the center of each cell and small English dates in the bottom-right corner.
- Highlight Saturdays and specific holidays with red text as per the reference UI.
- Take a `records` or `attendances`/`memos` prop to map backend data to specific dates on the grid.

### 3. Role-Specific Information Display
Inside the calendar cells, the information displayed will vary depending on the active user role:
- **Admin**: For each day, aggregate counts of total attendances will be displayed (e.g., "12 Present, 3 Absent"). Memos scheduled for that day will also be shown as a small list or badge.
- **Manager / Staff**: Only the user's specific attendance status (e.g., "Present", "Clock-in time") and their relevant memos will be shown inside the day's cell.

### 4. Replace `v-calendar` Integration
We will update the following pages to remove the existing `v-calendar` plugin and insert the new `NepaliCalendarGrid` component:
- `resources/js/Pages/Admin/Calendar/Index.vue`
- `resources/js/Pages/Manager/Attendance/Index.vue`
- `resources/js/Pages/Staff/Attendance/Index.vue`

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> Because `v-calendar` is being replaced here, do you want to keep `v-calendar` around for the *Date Pickers* in the Memo Create/Edit forms, or should we eventually replace those with a Nepali Date picker as well? (For now, we will leave the Memo Create/Edit forms alone and focus solely on the full-page grid calendar).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The backend currently sends data (like attendances and memos) using the English date `YYYY-MM-DD`. Our custom calendar component will take care of mapping those English dates into their corresponding Nepali dates dynamically on the frontend. Do you approve this frontend mapping approach, or would you prefer the backend to convert them before sending? (Frontend mapping is usually much faster).

